nodecode-wincred is a rewrite of Yicheng-Mark's Yicheng-Mark/hermes-windows-plugins:

  https://github.com/Yicheng-Mark/hermes-windows-plugins
  commit 5bad3fb2baf04ce6befecfefce6d14f4c9c98934
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Yicheng-Mark (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's read of the Windows Credential Manager, in Common Lisp. Its ctypes
binding of advapi32 is an SBCL alien binding of the same two calls, CredReadW and CredFree,
for a generic credential's target name in the current user's vault; its decoding of the blob
(UTF-8, UTF-16LE or UTF-16BE with a BOM, the NUL-count heuristic that tells the two apart,
and a value that decodes to neither skipped rather than injected) is ported byte for byte,
its ENV_VAR -> target mapping and its `wincred://` scheme are kept, and the same values end
up as environment variables of the process and its children. The plugin's map keys moved from
a JSON object to a list of ENV_VAR=target entries, the only shape this core's section reader
carries.

Left out: the Hermes secret-source orchestrator. Nodecode has no such seam, so where the
plugin resolved the map once at startup and the orchestrator applied it with its precedence
and provenance rules, here the map is applied by the cell at start (restored on stop) and by
`wincred_apply`, whose `override_existing` setting stands in for the orchestrator's. Values
are also readable one at a time through `wincred_read`, which the plugin never needed because
the agent only ever saw the environment. The plugin's Windows-only platform gate, read-only
surface, empty dependency set and no-subprocess, no-network, no-file-writes posture are
unchanged.
